---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import publication from '../../../../publications/research-monograph-en/publication.json';

const uniquePatterns = new Set(publication.chapters.flatMap((chapter) => chapter.patternIds)).size;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout title={`${publication.title} — Patrones IA`} description={publication.subtitle}>
  <section class="catalog-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">RESEARCH MONOGRAPH · EN · {publication.submissionReadiness.stage}</p>
    <h1>{publication.title}</h1>
    <p class="lead">{publication.subtitle}</p>
    <p>{publication.distinctiveContribution}</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/rubences/patrones_dise-o_ia/blob/main/publications/research-monograph-en/BOOK_PROPOSAL.md">Book Proposal</a>
      <a class="button" href="https://github.com/rubences/patrones_dise-o_ia/blob/main/publications/research-monograph-en/SUBMISSION_DOSSIER.md">Submission dossier</a>
      <a class="button" href="https://github.com/rubences/patrones_dise-o_ia/blob/main/publications/research-monograph-en/OUTLINE.md">Detailed outline</a>
      <a class="button" href={`${base}publications/readiness/`}>Publisher readiness</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="stat-grid">
      <div class="stat"><strong>{publication.chapters.length}</strong><span>research chapters</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><strong>{uniquePatterns}</strong><span>selected pattern IDs</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><strong>{publication.submissionReadiness.sampleChapters.length}</strong><span>sample chapters drafted</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><strong>Independent</strong><span>not a translation</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">THESIS</p><h2>From model behaviour to system architecture.</h2></div>
      <p>The monograph argues that AI-intensive systems need composable architectural patterns connecting probabilistic behaviour to deterministic controls, distributed execution, evidence, security and resilience.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="pattern-card"><span class="pattern-number">AGENTIC</span><h3>Control and MCP</h3><p>Orchestration, tools, protocol boundaries, validation, capability discovery and sandboxing.</p></article>
      <article class="pattern-card"><span class="pattern-number">DEPENDABILITY</span><h3>Reliable and secure AI</h3><p>Failure containment, recovery, authorization, adversarial testing, observability and semantic failure.</p></article>
      <article class="pattern-card"><span class="pattern-number">DISTRIBUTED</span><h3>Edge–Mesh–Cloud</h3><p>Original case studies for distributed placement, coordination, graceful degradation and high-dependability environments.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">ACQUISITIONS SAMPLES</p><h2>Two chapters show the book's two strongest differentiators.</h2></div>
      <p>One sample demonstrates the capability-boundary thesis around tools and MCP; the other demonstrates original Edge–Mesh–Cloud system architecture. Quantitative results remain explicitly pending until experiments are executed.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <a class="pattern-card" href="https://github.com/rubences/patrones_dise-o_ia/blob/main/publications/research-monograph-en/samples/03-tool-ecosystems-and-mcp.md"><span class="pattern-number">SAMPLE 03</span><h3>Tool Ecosystems and MCP</h3><p>Discovery, authorization, validation, sandboxing, sanitization and provenance as a capability architecture.</p></a>
      <a class="pattern-card" href="https://github.com/rubences/patrones_dise-o_ia/blob/main/publications/research-monograph-en/samples/10-edge-mesh-cloud-ai-architectures.md"><span class="pattern-number">SAMPLE 10</span><h3>Edge–Mesh–Cloud AI Architectures</h3><p>Placement, semantic health, resilience, fast/deliberative paths and a reproducible validation plan.</p></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">PROPOSED CONTENTS</p><h2>12 chapters organized by research questions.</h2></div>
      <p>The 102-pattern website remains the encyclopedic reference. The monograph selects and composes patterns to support a research argument.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="chapter-list">
      {publication.chapters.map((chapter) => (
        <article class="chapter-row">
          <span>{String(chapter.number).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
          <div><h3>{chapter.title}</h3><p>{chapter.originalContribution}</p><small>Pattern IDs: {chapter.patternIds.join(', ')}</small></div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">EDITORIAL ROUTES</p><h2>Candidates, not promises.</h2></div>
      <p>Series and imprint will be selected by editorial fit, peer-review process, rights, audience and distribution. No historical publisher ranking is treated as a guarantee.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="tags">{publication.publisherCandidates.map((publisher) => <span class="tag">{publisher}</span>)}</div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .chapter-list { display: grid; gap: .8rem; }
  .chapter-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 3rem 1fr; gap: 1rem; padding: 1.1rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 16px; background: rgba(18,27,45,.7); }
  .chapter-row > span { color: var(--accent-2); font-weight: 700; }
  .chapter-row h3 { margin: 0 0 .35rem; }
  .chapter-row p { margin: 0 0 .4rem; }
  .chapter-row small { color: var(--muted); }
</style>
